course: dictionary
lesson: 11326
title: Yoghurt, food from friendly bacteria
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word. They often give you clues to its meaning. «Yoghurt is milk heated to kill germs and then kept warm for hours with friendly bacteria that thicken it.» The clues are milk, heated and thicken, so yoghurt must be a thick food made from milk.
explain: Notice that yoghurt can mean the food itself or one small pot of it. «Three yoghurts are in the fridge» means three pots, because yoghurts is the plural for pots. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Context can also show you what something does. «After the final whistle, a sandwich, pasta, yoghurt or a glass of milk helps your muscles recover.» Yoghurt is a food you eat to refuel. Check your idea by swapping in another food, such as banana. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right kind of word.
fact: Yoghurt is a thick, creamy food made from milk.
fact: Yoghurt is made when helpful bacteria turn milk slightly sour, and this is why it is thick.
fact: A yoghurt is one small pot of yoghurt, and yoghurts means more than one pot.
fact: Yoghurt is spelled yoghurt or yogurt, and both spellings are correct.
fact: «Greek yoghurt», «natural yoghurt» and «frozen yoghurt» are all phrases you may see on a pot or in a shop.
exercise: «Yoghurt is milk heated to kill germs and then kept warm with friendly bacteria.» What is yoghurt? | A kind of bread baked in an oven | A crunchy snack made from potatoes | A fizzy drink made from fruit | *A thick, creamy food made from milk
exercise: «She ate two yoghurts after school.» How many pots of yoghurt did she eat? | None at all | Half a pot | *Two pots | One large bowl of milk
exercise: «Keep the yoghurt in the fridge and check the use-by date.» Why should yoghurt be kept in the fridge? | It makes the yoghurt crunchy | It makes the yoghurt sweeter | It turns the yoghurt into cheese | *It keeps the yoghurt from going off
test: What makes milk turn into yoghurt? | Cold air from the freezer | Plastic packaging | *Helpful bacteria | Sugar
test: «After sport, yoghurt helps your muscles recover.» According to this, what does yoghurt help after sport? | Your teeth to fall out | *Your muscles to recover | Your body to sleep faster | Your hair to grow
exam: «Three yoghurts are in the fridge.» What does yoghurts mean in this sentence? | Three glasses of milk | Three cheeses | Three friendly bacteria | *Three pots of yoghurt
